      "title": "How to Create an Online Class",
      "tags": ["materials", "Quality Assurance", "productive"],
      "description": "<p>Creating an online class involves planning, designing, and delivering learning content through a digital platform.<br>In this class, learners will explore how to structure an online course effectively — from defining objectives and developing modules to adding multimedia and interactive elements.<br>By the end of this course, participants will understand the key components of successful online learning and be able to design their own structured e-learning experience.</p><p><br><strong>Key Points:</strong></p><ol><li>Course Title: <i>How to Create an Online Class</i></li><li>Level: Intermediate</li><li>Duration: 5 Modules (Approx. 10 hours total)</li><li>Instructor: John Reynolds, M.Ed., Specialist in Digital Education</li><li>Language: English</li></ol>",
